---
import Guide from '../../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { CATEGORIES_EN } from '../../../data/pricing.en';
import { eurEn, ELEGXOS } from '../../../config';

// Αναζήτηση option με βάση id μέσα στον αγγλικό τιμοκατάλογο (ίδια ids/τιμές με pricing.ts)
const optionByIdEn = (id: string) =>
  CATEGORIES_EN.flatMap((c) => c.options).find((o) => o.id === id);

const match = optionByIdEn('auto-match')!;
const excel = optionByIdEn('auto-excel')!;
const day = optionByIdEn('auto-day')!;
const debt = optionByIdEn('auto-debt')!;
const spy = optionByIdEn('auto-spy')!;
const reviews = optionByIdEn('auto-reviews')!;
const loyalty = optionByIdEn('auto-loyalty')!;
const menu = optionByIdEn('auto-menu')!;

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Do I need to learn some new software?',
    a: 'No. The automations work with the tools you already use — you only see the result, usually as a message or a file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I get just one automation?',
    a: 'Yes. Each automation is separate — you pick the ones you need, one or several.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Am I locked into a contract?',
    a: 'No. The monthly automations have no commitment — you stop them whenever you want.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if something stops working?',
    a: "We fix it. That's what the support included in the monthly services covers.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does an automation cost?',
    a: `The smaller monthly ones start at ${eurEn(day.price)} per month. The one-off ones, like Organized Excel, start at ${eurEn(excel.price)}.`,
  },
];
---

<Guide
  lang="en"
  title="What are office automations? | PISMA"
  description="Automation means a routine office task gets done on its own — payment matching, debt reminders, reports. See what each one does."
  slug="what-are-automations"
  question="What are office automations?"
  sub="What each one does, in plain words — for business owners, not for techies."
  answer="An automation is a small system that takes over a routine office task and does it on its own, every time, without you thinking about it: it matches payments to invoices, sends reminders to people who owe you, updates the Excel, sends you a report. You only see the result."
  updated="2026-07-28"
  faq={faq}
>
  <h2>What does “automation” mean in practice?</h2>
  <p>
    It means a task you currently do by hand — again and again, every day or every week — is now
    done by a system, always the same way and always on time.
  </p>
  <p>
    You don’t need to learn anything new, and you don’t change how you work. The automation is
    set up once, works with the tools you already have, and you only see the result: a message,
    an updated file, a report.
  </p>

  <h2>Which automations does PISMA build?</h2>
  <p>Eight, each for one specific job. One sentence each:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>{match.label}</strong> — every payment that lands in your account finds its own
      invoice by itself. ({eurEn(match.price)} one-off)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{excel.label}</strong> — your transactions collect in one clean Excel that updates
      itself. ({eurEn(excel.price)} one-off)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{day.label}</strong> — every afternoon you get one message: what came in, what
      went out, what is pending. ({eurEn(day.price)} per month)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{debt.label}</strong> — everyone who owes you gets a polite reminder
      automatically, at the right moment. You only see who paid. ({eurEn(debt.price)} per month)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{spy.label}</strong> — you get a regular report on what your competition is doing:
      prices, offers, presence. ({eurEn(spy.price)} per month)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{reviews.label}</strong> — makes Google reviews pile up on their own. How?
      That part we only show live. ({eurEn(reviews.price)} per month)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{loyalty.label}</strong> — a QR code at the register: customers collect stamps on
      every visit and win a gift — and they come back. ({eurEn(loyalty.price)} per month)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{menu.label}</strong> — a QR code on the table: customers see your menu on their
      phone. Change prices and dishes with no reprints. ({eurEn(menu.price)} per month)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You will find more on how they all fit together on the
    <a href="/en/runs-by-itself/">Automation</a> page. For reviews specifically, there is also a
    separate guide: <a href="/en/guides/more-google-reviews/">how to get more reviews</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Do you pay once, or every month?</h2>
  <p>
    It depends on the automation. The ones that are set up once and then simply exist
    (like {excel.label}) are paid one-off. The ones that keep working for you
    (reminders, reports, reviews) have a small monthly price — and you stop them whenever you
    want, no contract.
  </p>
  <p>
    All prices are public, on the <a href="/en/pricing/">pricing page</a> — that is where you
    pick the ones you want and see the total.
  </p>

  <h2>Where do automations fit in your own work?</h2>
  <p>
    A simple way to think about it: which task do you do every week that is repetitive and
    boring? Figuring out which payment goes with which invoice? Calling the people who are
    late? Copying transactions into Excel? If any of these eats up your hours, there is an
    automation for it.
  </p>

  <h2>How does PISMA help?</h2>
  <p>
    If you don’t know where to start, the free <a href="/en/free-assessment/">PISMA Check</a>
    is the first step: in {ELEGXOS.minutes} minutes we map out together which routine tasks eat
    your time and which automations make sense for you — in writing, with priorities, with no
    commitment whatsoever.
  </p>
</Guide>
